            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery fistula related to dilatation of totally occluded vessel.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>835-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) is widely used to treat patients with coronary artery disease. Experience and improvement in catheters has led to its wider utilization. A case of coronary recanalization, complicated by coronary fistula created by an angioplasty guidewire, is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
